==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪˈfrʌntəri/|/ɛˈfrʌntəri/}}

===Etymology===
From late 17th century {{etyl|fr}} {{term|effronterie||lang=fr}}, from {{term|effronté||shameless, insolent|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|esfronté||lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|VL.|en}} *{{term||exfrontātus}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|exfrons|exfrōns|barefaced|lang=la}}, from [[prefix]] {{term|ex-||from|lang=la}} + {{term|frons|frōns|forehead|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|effronteries|-}}

# [[insolent]] and [[shameless]] [[audacity]]
#: ''We even had the '''effrontery''' to suggest that he should leave the country.''
# an [[act]] of insolent and shameless audacity
#: ''Any refusal to salute the president shall be counted as an '''effrontery'''.''

